,"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":41,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've delivered an edited network that lowers dev TTS from 44.8 to **44.3** veh-h, changing **352 of 7428 parameters** (limit 371). `weights.npz`, `NOTES.md` and `predictions.json` are in `work/`.\n\n**What I changed and why:** stop-line lanes hold only 3 vehicles, so a longer queue shows up only in the upstream halted-vehicle inputs. The trained network almost ignores those. In one recorded episode a full south left pocket blocked the upstream lane for 100 s, with halted vehicles growing from 2 to 8, while the network served other phases. I added scaled copies of existing input-weight columns into the 8 upstream-queue columns (first-layer weights only). Each halted upstream vehicle now counts as extra vehicles on the lane it is waiting for: 2 left-pocket + 1 straight for the upstream lane that feeds both, 3 through for the other. When nothing is halted upstream (about 96% of states), the output is exactly the same as the original's.\n\n**Simulator calls: 6 of 10.**\n\n| call | variant | low / nominal / high | mean |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| — | original | 34.5 / 44.9 / 55.0 | 44.8 |\n| 1 | upstream vehicle = 1 lane vehicle | 34.5 / 44.7 / 54.3 | 44.5 |\n| 2 | also count moving upstream vehicles | 34.9 / 45.1 / 54.7 | 44.9 |\n| 3 | = 2 lane vehicles | 34.5 / 44.6 / 53.7 | 44.25 |\n| 4 | = 3 lane vehicles | 34.5 / 44.5 / 54.5 | 44.5 |\n| 5 | **2, with through weighted 3 (delivered)** | 34.5 / 44.6 / 53.9 | **44.34** |\n| 6 | 5 + stop re-picking EW-left | 34.5 / 44.8 / 54.2 | 44.5 |\n\nCalls 3 and 5 are tied within noise. I kept 5 because, on recorded states, it serves through-lane spillbacks more often than the original does; call 3 serves them less often.\n\n**Test predictions:** low 34.5, nominal 44.7, high 54.2 veh-h. All the gain is at nominal and high demand.","ttft_ms":1008,"type":"result","duration_ms":1190117,"uuid":"e3cb1092-6202-4102-a2b0-604076a16929","ttft_